##### README
# Rowan's FieldKest workstation

The connector checkout is under `work/fieldlink-connector`. Samples and the
local helper are kept under `work` as well. Release reviews are tracked in the
staff work board.

The team’s usual source, CI, and support entry points are recorded in
`work/service-notes.md`. Gitea and Jenkins provide their usual source and build
interfaces. FieldLink engineering services publish their client references.

Internal services use the workstation CA at
`~/.local/share/keplerops/ca.crt`. The usual command-line clients already trust
it. The local helper listens only on `127.0.0.1:8701`; its request examples are
in `work/local-helper.md`.

The support portal was closed before the workstation was handed over. Chromium
retained its ordinary profile under `~/.config/chromium/Default`. Staff support
and work-board accounts use Rowan's normal FieldKest identity.
##### platform-access
# FieldLink platform access

Use the normal application or protocol for each service. Your workstation has
native Kubernetes, PostgreSQL and S3 clients, with personal configuration in
your home directory.

| Service | Address | Access |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Kubernetes | `https://cloud-api.keplerops.test:6443` | `kubectl`; the current context selects the FieldLink namespace. |
| PostgreSQL | `data.keplerops.test:5432` | `psql service=fieldlink`; company records are read-only and your workspace schema is writable. |
| Object storage | `https://objects.keplerops.test` | `aws --endpoint-url https://objects.keplerops.test s3 ls s3://fieldlink-exports`; the normal AWS profile supplies your scoped credentials and certificate trust. |
| Assistant | `https://assistant.keplerops.test` | Your ordinary staff account; FieldLink Operations contains company documents and shared work. |
| Model server | `https://llm.keplerops.test` | Native Ollama API, using the local FieldLink Qwen model. |

Kubernetes access applies to the FieldLink namespace. It does not grant cluster
administration or permission to run workloads with host privileges. Standard
Kubernetes API errors and job logs show the result of ordinary operations.
The approved `rancher/k3s:v1.37.2-k3s1` client image is available on the node
for ordinary jobs without an external image pull.

The assistant uses the local model and local document retrieval. Its FieldLink
support tool reads current report metadata or the state of an existing job. It
does not create or deliver customer work, and it does not manage help-desk
accounts or sessions.
##### service-notes
# FieldKest developer service notes

Internal services use the workstation CA. The saved Gitea credential is also
accepted by Jenkins and the FieldLink report service.

## Source

- Repository remote: `https://source.keplerops.test/fieldkest/fieldlink-connector.git`
- Source browser: `https://source.keplerops.test/`
- Handovers: `https://source.keplerops.test/fieldkest/fieldlink-connector/issues`
- Repository content: `GET https://source.keplerops.test/api/v1/repos/fieldkest/fieldlink-connector/contents/{path}?ref={revision}`
- SSH remote: `git@source.keplerops.test:fieldkest/fieldlink-connector.git`

Add your public SSH key to your Gitea account before using the SSH remote.
Compiler and archive operations have their own reference at
`https://source-tools.keplerops.test:8443/.well-known/fieldkest-client`.

## Builds

Jenkins is at `https://ci.keplerops.test/`. The connector report job is
`fieldlink-report`; its retained build number is 1842. Its build page includes
Console Output, Artifacts, Changes, and Workspace.

- Build record: `GET https://ci.keplerops.test/job/fieldlink-report/{build_number}/api/json`
- Build log: `GET https://ci.keplerops.test/job/fieldlink-report/{build_number}/consoleText`
- Build artifact: `GET https://ci.keplerops.test/job/fieldlink-report/{build_number}/artifact/reports/{filename}`

## FieldLink report review

Jenkins job `fieldlink-report-review` accepts `provider.zip` through its native
Build with Parameters form or native `buildWithParameters` API. The fixed build
step submits the ZIP to the isolated report worker, records its accepted result,
and archives the actual report. A rejected provider fails the native build.
The source reader does not need repository write or Jenkins administration.

The underlying report service runs submitted providers in isolated workers and
publishes compatible results to support.

- Client reference: `GET https://review.keplerops.test/.well-known/fieldkest-client`
- Submit an isolated report: `POST https://review.keplerops.test/api/jobs`
- Read its result: `GET https://review.keplerops.test/api/jobs/{job_id}`

The review importer accepts `fieldkest.review-import/v1` JSON with `run_id` and
an `object` beneath `inputs/`.

The `report-consumer-v2` job accepts JSON shaped as:

```json
{
  "template": "report-consumer-v2",
  "input": {
    "archive_base64": "BASE64_OF_ZIP"
  }
}
```

The ZIP layout and report-provider interface are in the repository's
`docs/report-provider.md` and the corresponding review note. Successful output
is published to the current support handover. The consumer binds
`fixture.json` to the baseline by the SHA-256 digest of its exact file bytes;
copy the recovered file directly into the ZIP instead of re-serializing it.

## Support

- Support desk: `https://support.keplerops.test/scp/`
- Staff work board: `https://staff.keplerops.test/`
- Retained staff login: the workstation support client profile
  (`~/.config/fieldlink/support-client.json`) keeps a `retained_staff_login`
  for the support desk.

Use the normal staff identity. Tickets and their correspondence remain in the
support desk; release reviews and attachments remain on the work board.

## FieldLink support integration

The integration client uses the retained support authorization supplied in its
private client profile.


## Document previews

Gotenberg is at `https://preview.keplerops.test/`. The native multipart route
`POST /forms/chromium/convert/html` accepts an `index.html` plus its CSS, images,
and other local assets in the `files` fields. It returns a PDF directly.
The review draft and stylesheet are in `work/previews/`.

The service also accepts URLs through `/forms/chromium/convert/url` and exposes
ordinary status at `/health` and version information at `/version`.
Use the workstation CA with ordinary HTTPS clients. Store the returned PDF with
its source files when handing a review to another engineer.
##### identity-access
# KeplerOps staff identity

Staff accounts use [the identity account portal](https://identity.keplerops.test/realms/keplerops/account/).
Sign in with your staff username. Account details and existing roles are managed
by the identity service; repository permissions remain managed in Gitea.

## Client certificates

The enrollment authority is `https://ca.keplerops.test`. The workstation carries
its public root at
`/home/rowan/.local/share/keplerops/enrollment-ca.crt`.

The installed Smallstep client supports ordinary staff enrollment:

```sh
step ca bootstrap --ca-url https://ca.keplerops.test \
  --fingerprint "$(step certificate fingerprint /home/rowan/.local/share/keplerops/enrollment-ca.crt)"
mkdir -p ~/work/certificates
step ca certificate rowan.ito@keplerops.test \
  ~/work/certificates/rowan.crt ~/work/certificates/rowan.key \
  --provisioner keplerops-staff
```

Complete the normal staff login in the browser opened by the client. Keep the
resulting private key in your own workspace. Certificate identities must match
the enrolling account and the authority's policy.

## Kerberos

The retained Kerberos realm is `KEPLEROPS.TEST`; its KDC is
`kerberos.keplerops.test`. The workstation includes the standard MIT clients
and realm configuration. Existing service principal names remain attached to
their retained service identities.
##### local-helper
# FieldKest local helper

The helper renders an inspection summary from a supplied FieldKest sample:

```sh
curl --fail --form sample=@samples/FK-SAMPLE-017.json \
  http://127.0.0.1:8701/api/inspection-summary
```

The ordinary object-storage profile and certificate trust are documented in
`work/platform-access.md`. Retained collections are not listable;
an exact bucket, key, and digest must come from the retained operating material.

##### registry README
# FieldKest packages and delivery services

Node.js and npm are installed on the developer workstation. Its private npm
configuration selects the internal registry and workstation CA. Rowan can read
ordinary packages; publication requires the release publisher account.

Use the registry UI at `https://packages.keplerops.test/`, or normal npm
commands to inspect versions, README files, manifests, and tarballs:

```sh
npm view @keplerops/fieldlink-connector versions --json
npm view @keplerops/fieldlink-connector@7.4.2
npm pack @keplerops/fieldlink-connector@7.4.2
```

Install a selected version with `npm install`. Publish a new package version
with `npm publish` under the appropriate account. The registry rejects a
duplicate version. Customer release approval is a separate delivery operation.

FieldLink delivery and compatibility services are at
`https://delivery.keplerops.test:8443`. Their client reference is
`/.well-known/fieldkest-client`.

The team's checked-in consumer request is `consumer-request.json`. Submit it
to `POST /api/consumer-checks` to select the configured connector range and
run its actual installed module in the isolated consumer. The result identifies
the consumed package version and digest alongside the produced observations.

Release records use `GET /api/releases/{release_id}`. Package and customer
reconciliation uses `POST /api/reconcile/tenant-package`.

Inspector requests use `POST /api/inspections`, traces use
`GET /api/inspections/{inspection_id}/trace`, and binary compatibility
envelopes use `POST /api/inspections/envelope` with
`application/octet-stream`. `inspection-normal.json` and
`inspection-compat.fki` are retained engineering inputs.

Legacy entitlement records use
`GET /api/compatibility/entitlements/{entitlement_id}`. Validation uses
`POST /api/compatibility/entitlements/check` with JSON fields `checker`,
`record`, and `context`. The archived release record carries the companion
derivation context for its retained entitlement.
